      "description": "200 L domestic-hot-water buffer, water-filled, installed inside the thermal envelope. EnergyADE 3.0 has no native attribute for in-envelope vs outside-envelope placement, so this is recorded here in the description. The `preparation_temperature` (32 °C) is read from the owner-occupier's thermal-storage stratification diagram (charged-state hot-side temperature), close to the heat pump's 31 °C operation temperature — i.e. this is a low-temperature buffer driven by the heat pump rather than a 60 °C+ DHW tank with separate legionella protection.",
